              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "leelee29"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was an awesome recipe! I used skinless chicken breasts &amp; made it in the oven in a Pyrex dish. I sprayed the dish with olive oil spray. I used BBQ sauce &amp; added the mustard &amp;a fresh lime wedge(instead of lemon) in the sauce....it was sooooo delicious!! The chicken was moist....I paired it with homemade mashed potatoes &amp; fresh broccoli. Mmmmmmmm mmmmm mmmmmm Good!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tim Westfield"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this on Father's Day weekend. It was very good. I used organic bacon and I like to have things a little spicier so I cut back on the ketchup but added 1/2 a cup of Chilli sauce. It turned out very good and did not drown out the maple syrup taste. I also doubled the garlic. Cooking the bacon first is a very good idea and I also seared the chicken breasts in a frying pan first. I'll definitely be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-06-22T10:45:20.227Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! I didn't salt/pepper the chicken prior to the grill as I decided to marinate the chicken for 15-ish minutes with the basting ingredients while I baked the bacon prior to wrapping the chicken with it. I didn't put lemon, or chives, on it afterwards. It turned out very tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-14T18:26:59.837Z"
          },
